UnitClPoolTape::FetchSecondsPerLiquidityCumulativeAt
├── when the target timestamp is gte the current block timestamp
│   └── it returns the live secondsPerLiquidityCumulativeX128 from the pool
└── when the target timestamp is lt the current block timestamp
    ├── when the pool oracle still has the target timestamp
    │   └── it returns the pool oracle value at the target
    ├── when the pool oracle reverts with a string
    │   ├── when the error is OLD
    │   │   ├── it interpolates between the newest committed observation and the live value
    │   │   ├── when the cumulative wrapped between the commit and the live value
    │   │   │   └── it interpolates across the wrap
    │   │   └── when the target timestamp is lte the newest committed observation
    │   │       └── it returns the observation secondsPerLiquidityCumulativeX128 value
    │   └── when the error is not OLD
    │       └── it reverts
    └── when the pool oracle reverts with something else
        └── it reverts
